==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[go]]-[[ahead]]}}

# [[approval|Approval]], [[agreement]], or [[instruction]] to begin or [[proceed]].
#: ''You can start as soon as you get the '''go-ahead''' from the president.''

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|head=[[go]]-[[ahead]]}}

# {{lb|en|comparable}} [[progressive|Progressive]]; exerting leadership.
#* {{quote-text|year=1906|author=Arthur Lincoln Haydon|title=The Book of the V. C.|page=150|passage=This turbulent ruler was a very '''go-ahead''' monarch indeed. He organised a splendid army, well-drilled and well-equipped with modern arms}}
# {{lb|en|sports|not comparable}} A [[score]] which gives the scoring team or player the lead in the game.
#: ''The pitcher gave up the '''go-ahead''' run in the top of the ninth inning.''

